#!/bin/bash
# =============================================================================
#  slipmat  —  bulletproof video ripper for macOS 12+ (re-encodes need Apple Silicon)
#  The engine behind the SLIPMAT shortcut suite. Design notes live in the
#  comments beside the code they explain.
# =============================================================================
#
#  THE ONE RULE: a downloaded HLS file can play perfectly in VLC yet stutter in
#  QuickTime, because the source's presentation timestamps (PTS) are jittery and
#  QuickTime is strict where VLC is tolerant. The cure is a constant-frame-rate
#  (CFR) re-encode, done FROM AN MKV SCRATCH FILE at the source's exact detected
#  frame rate. The trick is detecting which files need it without being fooled by
#  probes that read "clean."  (Memory: mkv-is-reencode-input, duration-time-lies.)
#
#  PIPELINE:
#     metadata probe -> LIVE? --yes--> capture direct->mp4 (Ctrl-C safe). done.
#                        |no
#                        v
#     non-HLS QT-ready -> DIRECT to mp4 (fast path, audio-verified; no mkv/detect)
#     otherwise: download -> MKV scratch -> codec-route -> DETECT (sorted-PTS):
#        clean + mp4-friendly codec  -> lossless remux mkv->mp4 (seconds)
#        defective OR vp9/av1/webm   -> CFR re-encode from mkv (HEVC, -q:v)
#     -> verify -> self-documenting name -> receipt
#
#  USAGE:  slipmat video <URL|file> [RES] [MODE]   — or the shorthand:  slipmat <URL> <MODE>
#     RES   = 480 | 720 | 1080 | max | ask  (default: max)
#     MODE  = best | auto | studio          (default: auto)
#        best   : the BEST QuickTime-playable stream, UNCAPPED, no questions
#                 (defective HLS >720 still auto-downscales to 720).
#        auto   : fix at the chosen RES, no questions (ask = the picker menu).
#        studio : interactive — file info, downscale?, then ONE recipe table
#                 (V3.6: q25/30/35/40 + fps twins, sampled per-file estimates,
#                 row 0 keeps lossless on clean sources; V4.0: rows = quality
#                 flags with an ETA column, `1f`/`f` = fast flags), delete-original?
#     Shorthand: `slipmat <url> best` = auto-best · `auto`/`studio` imply `ask`.
#     Self-check: `slipmat doctor` (the wrapper adds audio + Spotify checks); `--doctor` here runs the engine's own.
#
#  Target: ffmpeg 8.1.x + videotoolbox, yt-dlp 2026.05+, bash 3.2 (stock macOS).
# =============================================================================

